{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And He said.</b> Now we find mute corresponding to the setting of the mouth, and blind corresponding to seeing, and the deaf alone remains with no counterpart. But the truth is that the word seeing corresponds to the deaf and the blind, as written: \"open of ears\" (Isaiah 42:20), \"to open blind eyes\" (ibid. 7)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:31:28.899583032Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}